## Why This Is Asked
This problem introduces a dynamic programming angle where subarrays are weighted by their block index. It tests the ability to transform interval sums into prefix sums, derive a two-dimensional DP over position and block count, and implement solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Prefix sums for O(1) interval sum computation
- 2D DP over position and block count
- Solution reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k); Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScorePartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = [0];
  for (let x of A) P.push(P[P.length-1] + x);
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    dp[i][1] = P[i];
  }

  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
        const score = dp[p][t-1] + (P[i] - P[p]) * t;
        if (score > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = score;
          parent[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct partitions
  const partitions = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = parent[end][t];
    partitions.unshift([start+1, end]);
    end = start;
  }

  return { maxScore: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests your ability to structure a dynamic programming solution for exact-k resource selection with non-overlapping intervals. It requires combining weighted interval scheduling with a prefix DP over both task count and index, along with binary search for efficient predecessor lookup and clean reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with exact k constraint
- Prefix DP over tasks (i) and count (t)
- Precomputing p[i] via binary search for O(log n) lookups
- Backtracking through DP table for reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function weightedIntervalScheduling(tasks, K) {
  // Sort by end time
  tasks.sort((a, b) => a.end - b.end);
  const n = tasks.length;

  // Precompute p[i] - last non-overlapping task
  const ends = tasks.map(t => t.end);
  const p = new Array(n).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let lo = 0, hi = i - 1, res = -1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = Math.floor) / 2((lo + hi);
      if (tasks[mid].end <= tasks[i].start) {
        res = mid;
        lo = mid + 1;
      } else {
        hi = mid - 1;
      }
    }
    p[i] = res;
  }

  // DP table: dp[i][t] = max value using first i tasks for t selections
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(K + 1).fill(0));

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= K; t++) {
      // Skip task i-1
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      // Take task i-1
      if (p[i - 1] !== -1) {
        dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[p[i - 1] + 1][t - 1] + tasks[i - 1].value);
      } else if (t === 1) {
        dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], tasks[i - 1].value);
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const chosen = [];
  let i = n, t = K;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    if (dp[i][t] === dp[i - 1][t]) {
      i--;
    } else {
      chosen.push(i - 1);
      const prev = p[i - 1];
      i = prev + 1;
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][K], chosenTasks: chosen.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model partitioning with a simple per-block objective and reconstruct optimal cuts. It reveals DP formulation, range queries, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP across two dimensions (prefix and blocks)
- Range maximum precomputation or on-the-fly tracking
- Backpointers for path reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPartitionCostMax(A, m){
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const rangeMax = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let cur = 0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      cur = Math.max(cur, A[j]);
      rangeMax[i][j] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=1;j<=Math.min(i,m);j++){
      for(let t=j-1; t<=i-1; t++){
        const val = dp[t][j-1] + rangeMax[t][i-1];
        if(val < dp[i][j]){
          dp[i][j] = val;
          par[i][j] = t;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, j = m;
  while(j>0){
    const t = par[i][j];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = t;
    j--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][m], partitions: cuts};
}
```

